    "section_summary": {
      "type": "string",
      "extract_value": "This abstract describes two studies. Study 1, a cross-sectional study of 215 female UK students, investigated the indirect negative association between appearance goals and body image through introjected regulation. Study 2, an experimental study with 165 participants, manipulated guilt related to exercise and appearance goals, finding that increased guilt was associated with increased body anxiety for participants in the guilt condition.",
